{"title":"1954 AHSME Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_19\">Problem 19</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 19\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the three points of contact of a circle inscribed in a triangle are joined, the angles of the resulting triangle: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/9/0a90d14972e5a6b5253061c5937f811fa18d3a50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{are always equal to }60^\\circ\\\\ \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{are always one obtuse angle and two unequal acute angles}\\\\ \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{are always one obtuse angle and two equal acute angles}\\\\ \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{are always acute angles}\\\\ \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{are always unequal to each other}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"455\" height=\"96\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For the sake of clarity, let the outermost triangle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> with incircle tangency points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/1/c916b8759df7c2b95e696adf2d20c5abdef98ea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A=\\alpha$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/8/c78cad686fc192728718fdef92cbba82daf3974f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B=\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/f/e8f2628c7bd8aba6794daadad02ce8f46d94c15c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AFE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/c/4bc4a1ecf2193896680e5e73b698d50e779548b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BDF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> are isosceles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/2/c421815db91eefe8b6f71e8b81854869bfde9727.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AFE=\\frac{180-\\alpha}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"143\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/6/996a5f7127bee6e15e84f38920ba60e5fe90f10e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BFD=\\frac{180-\\beta}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"144\" height=\"38\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05db8e32122e6963526744d0d7954f4165cbd44f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DFE=180-\\frac{180-\\alpha}{2}-\\frac{180-\\beta}{2}=\\frac{\\alpha+\\beta}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"354\" height=\"38\" />, and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/e/b3eab9622343394b204df0ce395eb2f6b5f0f672.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha + \\beta &lt;180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"102\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/5/3e5cdb99d966ecc33e6d1c4dd08268fe6427f418.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DFE$\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" /> is acute. \n</p><p>The same method applies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/1/ab1e3a7476da92b5f4c7541dbd0c89a981482809.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FED$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/1/d8170c8e9ea492c189edd91dde7c5b8eeaa68bd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FDE$\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" />, which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/872e3b09425c9659d782119a543dc858aa520a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is acute - hence our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/8/25809e4f87f20a2ee949878bc603b9eda09422ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME\" title=\"1954 AHSME\">1954 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1954 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1954 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1954\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1954 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1954 AHSME Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1954 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1954 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1954 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1954 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1954 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1954 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1954 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1954_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1954 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?ti